+<header class="hero">
+  <div class="kicker"><span class="ver" data-version="0.6.0">delixcrew 0.6.0</span><span>Claude Code plugin · MIT</span></div>
+  <h1>delix<span>Crew</span></h1>
+  <p class="thesis">Spec first. Agents write the code. <em>A human makes the final call.</em></p>
+  <p class="lede">The main session that runs the work is the <strong>lead</strong>. The lead asks you one question at a time (this interview is called the grill) and writes a tech spec from your answers. It then splits the work into <strong>cards</strong>: small, independent units of work. Each card goes to a separate implementer session working in its own worktree. Review agents that cannot change files check the result.</p>
+  <p class="lede">The work stops at two points and waits for a human. These points are <strong>gates</strong>: at Gate 1 the spec is approved, at Gate 2 the PR is merged. The rules are not left to the agent's good intentions; Claude Code itself enforces them: hooks block forbidden actions and tool lists limit what each agent can do. This page calls that control layer the <strong>harness</strong>.</p>
+  <ol class="rail" aria-label="Main flow">
+    <li>start</li><li class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</li>
+    <li>spec</li><li class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</li>
+    <li class="gate"><svg class="ico"><use href="assets/icons.svg#i-lock"/></svg>Gate 1 · spec approval</li><li class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</li>
+    <li>dispatch</li><li class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</li>
+    <li>implement</li><li class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</li>
+    <li>review</li><li class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</li>
+    <li class="gate"><svg class="ico"><use href="assets/icons.svg#i-lock"/></svg>Gate 2 · merge</li><li class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</li>
+    <li>close</li>
+  </ol>
