+<section id="idea">
+  <div class="sec-head">
+    <div class="eyebrow"><svg class="ico"><use href="assets/icons.svg#i-doc"/></svg>Core idea</div>
+    <h2>A software team's division of labour instead of a single-session loop</h2>
+    <p>Roles replace the loop of "open, pick a folder, read the history, continue". What each role can do is limited by its tool list and by hooks.</p>
+  </div>
+  <div class="principles">
+    <article class="pr agent"><h3><svg class="ico"><use href="assets/icons.svg#i-doc"/></svg>Spec first</h3><p>The grill asks one question at a time and adds a recommendation to each. Requirements are written to be testable, in <code>SHALL</code> and <code>WHEN/THEN</code> form. What is out of scope is stated explicitly.</p></article>
+    <article class="pr agent"><h3><svg class="ico"><use href="assets/icons.svg#i-bot"/></svg>Agents write the code</h3><p>The implementer works in its own worktree. It changes only the files the card allows (the Files list). It writes a failing test first and cannot change existing tests.</p></article>
+    <article class="pr human"><h3><svg class="ico"><use href="assets/icons.svg#i-lock"/></svg>A human decides</h3><p>At Gate 1 the spec or card is approved, at Gate 2 the PR is merged. The riskiest cards (Tier 3) also need an explicit security approval. The lead never runs <code>gh pr merge</code>.</p></article>
+    <article class="pr hk-p"><h3><svg class="ico"><use href="assets/icons.svg#i-shield"/></svg>Claude Code enforces the rules</h3><p>Review agents (reviewers) have no write tool in their <code>tools</code> list. Hooks block writes to protected paths (auth, secrets, CI, deploy) and to existing test files. Because of the Stop hook, the implementer cannot finish until the tests pass.</p></article>
+  </div>
+  <p class="src"><b>Source:</b> README.md (intro, Roles) · skills/review/SKILL.md §4 · hooks/hooks.json</p>
+</section>
