+    <div class="notes">
+      <div class="note limit">
+        <h3><svg class="ico"><use href="assets/icons.svg#i-shield"/></svg>Known limits</h3>
+        <ul>
+          <li>write_gate does not see what is written through Bash (<code>echo &gt;</code>, <code>sed -i</code>, <code>tee</code>). bash_gate catches only redirects, <code>cp</code>, <code>mv</code> and <code>tee</code> into a protected path. To cover this gap, the qa agent counts a change to the card or to <code>docs/delix/**</code> in the diff as a finding.</li>
+          <li>The hooks close the known send paths, not every path. A command built from base64, a wrapper written to a file or an HTTP request without gh can get past pattern matching. The README suggests adding <code>permissions.deny</code> to your own <code>settings.json</code>.</li>
+          <li>Claude Code ignores the <code>permissionMode</code>, <code>hooks</code> and <code>mcpServers</code> fields in plugin agent definitions. That is why the constraints live in the <code>tools</code> list and in <code>hooks.json</code>.</li>
+          <li>Cards that arrive in an archive carrying its own <code>.git</code> are an open case, tracked in issue #17. T007 closed tracked and symlinked cards.</li>
+        </ul>
+      </div>
+      <div class="note">
+        <h3><span class="pill ag">0.6.0</span>Triage hook rules</h3>
+        <p>In every session bash_gate denies <code>triage.py apply</code> and running <code>triage.py</code> under <code>script</code>, <code>expect</code>, <code>unbuffer</code> or <code>pty.spawn</code>. It also denies <code>gh issue close|reopen|lock|…</code>, <code>gh label</code> and writing <code>gh api</code> calls (<code>-f</code>, <code>--input</code>, <code>graphql</code>, a method other than GET) aimed at delixcrew. write_gate denies direct writes into the triage record directory. As with feedback, only the known paths are closed.</p>
+      </div>
+    </div>
