+      <dl>
+        <div><dt>Every session</dt><dd><code>feedback.py send</code> is denied, and so are the <code>script</code>, <code>expect</code>, <code>unbuffer</code> and <code>pty.spawn</code> wrappers. <code>gh issue create|comment|edit</code> and <code>gh api … issues</code> calls aimed at delixcrew are denied too. The triage write paths are closed as well (see the note above).</dd></div>
+        <div><dt>Reviewer</dt><dd>security runs only scanners (gitleaks, semgrep, pip-audit, trivy, …) and git read commands; the other reviewers cannot use Bash.</dd></div>
+        <div><dt>Implementer</dt><dd>Shell writes into a protected path are denied. Before <code>git commit</code>, <code>gitleaks protect</code> runs on the staged changes; a finding stops the commit. Without gitleaks a note goes to <code>.delix/warnings.log</code>.</dd></div>
+      </dl>
+    </article>
+    <article class="hook">
+      <h3>stop_gate.py</h3>
+      <p class="when">Stop · 540 s per command</p>
+      <dl>
+        <div><dt>Implementer only</dt><dd>Runs <code>test_command</code> and <code>extra_checks</code> and writes the output to <code>.delix/test-result.txt</code>. If one fails, the exit code is 2 and the implementer cannot finish.</dd></div>
+        <div><dt>Way out</dt><dd>If the report says <code>NEEDS_CONTEXT</code> or <code>BLOCKED</code>, the implementer can stop. <code>stop_hook_active</code> prevents an endless loop.</dd></div>
+        <div><dt>Limit</dt><dd>Only these local commands run. The lead runs the card's verification command and the full suite during review.</dd></div>
+      </dl>
+    </article>
+  </div>
+  <p class="src"><b>Source:</b> hooks/hooks.json · scripts/write_gate.py · scripts/bash_gate.py · scripts/stop_gate.py · scripts/common.py (card_path) · README.md (Known limits, Remaining risk) · CHANGELOG 0.5.0 (T007) · README.md (Triage) · CHANGELOG 0.6.0</p>
+</section>
