+<section id="glossary">
+  <div class="sec-head">
+    <div class="eyebrow"><svg class="ico"><use href="assets/icons.svg#i-book"/></svg>Glossary</div>
+    <h2>Short glossary</h2>
+  </div>
+  <dl class="gloss">
+    <div><dt>card</dt><dd>One unit of work, in <code>docs/delix/tasks/T&lt;nnn&gt;-&lt;slug&gt;.md</code>. It holds the goal, the Files list, Interfaces, the verification command and the report contract. Files lists do not overlap between cards.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>wave</dt><dd>A group of cards opened together, at most <code>max_parallel</code> (3). A card that touches the same file as another, or depends on another card, goes to the next wave. Kept in <code>STATE.json.waves</code>.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>tier</dt><dd>The risk axis that sets the gates (1–3). It looks at the file path, the action and external content. A separate axis from size (S/M/L, process weight).</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>gate</dt><dd>A point where a human decides. At Gate 1 the spec or card is approved, at Gate 2 the PR is merged. A Tier 3 card also needs a security approval. Automatic checks such as tests, CI and gitleaks are gates too (deterministic gates): a machine decides, and they run before the LLM review.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>drift</dt><dd>The gap between the spec and the merged code: REQs not implemented, or behaviour not in the spec. The architect looks for it at close; findings go to the open items in STATUS.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>escalation</dt><dd>When review rounds pass <code>max_review_rounds</code> (3), the card becomes <code>escalated</code>. The user picks: a stronger model, a narrower scope, or accept.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>worktree</dt><dd>The implementer's own git working tree on the card branch. Diffs and remote tests are taken from the branch's commit SHA, not from the directory.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>K decision</dt><dd>A numbered decision record (K1, K2, …), kept in STATUS and SPEC and marked "reversible" or "one-way".</dd></div>
+  </dl>
+  <p class="src"><b>Source:</b> templates/task-card.md · skills/dispatch/SKILL.md §2 · skills/start/SKILL.md §2 · skills/close/SKILL.md §3 · skills/review/SKILL.md §1, §3 · skills/spec/SKILL.md (Rules)</p>
+</section>
